what that looks like.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.420
- The issue of China ruling
over autonomous regions

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.770
is controversial.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:58.200
So, what are China's autonomous regions?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.360
And, are they really all that autonomous?

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.130
- This is the map that most people

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.990
are familiar with when
they think of China.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.090
But, this outline doesn't
tell you the whole story,

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:09.960
because nearly half of this
land is considered autonomous,

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.160
super jargony term.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.060
What does that even mean?

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.730
There are over 56 ethnicities in China.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.310
Most of them concentrated
far away from Beijing,

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:20.250
like over here in Tibet,
or over here in Xinjiang.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.240
When those communist leaders

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.120
were setting up their
new unified China empire,

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.010
they kind of admitted like, okay,

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.020
there are a lot of
cultures, and languages,

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.150
and identities within this country,

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.430
we should let these
people govern themselves.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:34.170
Not entirely, of course.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.270
They'd still have to answer to
Beijing with certain things,

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:39.480
but they would have
autonomy, autonomous regions,

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:42.330
but many of these semi autonomous
regions, like Xinjiang,

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.100
Tibet, and southern Mongolia,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.660
these places were never originally a part

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:47.670
of any conception of China.

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:51.420
They were forcefully absorbed
by the Chinese communist party

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.130
during its nation building project

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:54.990
like in the past 70 years.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.940
Okay, let's get specific here.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.910
Xinjiang is a region that
is very far from Beijing,

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.320
not just geographically,

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.078
but also culturally.

00:12:03.078 --> 00:12:06.330
It is a huge region,
roughly the size of Alaska,

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.500
has 25 million people,

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.200
and half of those people
identify as Uyghur

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.830
which are mostly Muslims who
are from a Turkic descent

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.750
not like a Han Chinese descent.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.280
They come from a different culture.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.864
The street signs are not
in any Chinese language.

00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:22.110
They're in like the
Uyghur Turkic language.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:25.200
The architecture looks a lot
more at home in like Istanbul

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.210
than it does in Beijing.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.200
And, five times a day,

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.270
the streets fill with the sound of prayer.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.090
Xinjiang was an independent
Republic twice before,

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:34.980
but eventually it was overthrown by China.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.770
Eight years after China grabbed Xinjiang,

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.840
the Chinese government did the same thing

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.850
to an even more remote region

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:44.703
at the highest plateau
in the world, Tibet.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.490
They annexed this place

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:50.490
that is three times the size of Texas.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.340
It has its own very distinct
language, culture, identity,

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:56.640
and does not identify
or connect with Beijing.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:57.900
And, back in the day, again,

00:12:57.900 --> 00:12:59.340
when China wasn't rich and powerful,

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.010
they couldn't really wrangle these regions

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.987
until suddenly they got rich really fast.

00:13:04.987 --> 00:13:06.630
- [Female Reporter 2] Second in GDP,

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:09.180
only to the United States.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.220
- And, for the past 30 to 40 years,

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.840
China has been pouring money

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:15.090
and people into these two regions

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:17.490
to make them more like China.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.050
It's kind of like the geopolitical version

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:19.980
of gentrification.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.930
It's basically where non-Chinese societies

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:26.070
are subsumed by societal
norms of Han Chinese culture,

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.920
because of a bunch of
militarization and money.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:31.920
So, in Tibet, you see this
in the Tibetan schools

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.810
that are only teaching in Mandarin

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.700
not in the traditional Tibetan language

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.200
or you see it in Xinjiang,

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.880
where the mosques are torn down

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.320
for being too Islamic,

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.500
and are rebuilt in
traditional Chinese styles.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.780
Oh, and it starts to get a lot worse.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:48.690
In Xinjiang, the Uyghurs
are literally taken away

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:50.040
by the millions

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.900
and forced into concentration camps

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:55.470
where they're supposedly
forcibly taught Chinese values.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.670
The government is involved

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.860
in a mass sterilization project

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:01.140
where they are forcibly inserting IUDs

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:02.730
and other birth control forms

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.340
to basically run them into extinction.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:09.780
And, not just like 10 people,
like millions of people.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.940
China originally gave
these people autonomy,

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:14.700
because they recognized that
they had their own culture

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:15.840
and they wanted to retain it.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:18.570
But, now, they've totally
thrown that deal out the window.

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.880
The way this presents most
commonly in these regions

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.910
is just the presence
of military and police.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:25.530
There are checkpoints everywhere.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:28.890
There's restricted movement,
there's constant surveillance.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:31.170
And, every year that
passes by becomes harder.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:33.960
These people resist, they fight back.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.610
They commit acts of terror.

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:39.210
And, in response, China sends
more military, more police,

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.430
and more surveillance equipment.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:46.430
In 2018, China spent $10
billion in security in Xinjiang.

00:14:47.026 --> 00:14:50.040
That's almost double the year before

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:53.130
and 10 times as much as
it was 10 years previous.

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:56.940
3 billion of those dollars go
into these reeducation camps.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.950
That's four times more
than the previous year.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:00.240
I mean, it's ramping up.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:02.130
They're pouring money into these regions.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:07.130
Per person, China spends 3,100
Yuan on security in Tibet,

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.621
2,400 in Xinjiang,

00:15:09.621 --> 00:15:10.536
per person.

00:15:10.536 --> 00:15:14.070
Compare that to the national
average of 763 Yuan per person

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:17.670
and you can see that every
single person in these regions

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.370
is worth a lot more in terms of the cost

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:21.750
of making them assimilate.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.126
So, the question is why?

00:15:23.126 --> 00:15:24.540
Why is China doing this?

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.760
Why are they investing so much money

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:30.900
into occupying and forcibly
assimilating these people?

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.520
Well, there are several geopolitical

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.020
and economic reasons why

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:36.030
the communist party wants to do this.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.040
First off, the resources.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.340
Xinjiang produces 87% of the
country's cotton, for example.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.390
And, when it comes to Tibet,

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.430
you can see that they provide a buffer

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.080
between China and India.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:49.920
Tibet also has the largest
fresh water supply in the world,

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.810
given where they are, so high up.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.580
China also uses these regions

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.460
as a part of their big
infrastructure initiative,

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.630
the belt and road initiative.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:00.300
They use infrastructure
to connect these regions

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:03.540
to continue to fortify their
economic standing in the world.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.180
But, I believe the real
reason is this myth,

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:08.010
this myth of a united China,

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.860
because a United China is a strong China.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:14.310
A divided China is a chaotic China.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:16.890
This has been the
rallying cry for 70 years,

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:20.160
but it's not just assimilation
within their borders.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.340
This myth has also fueled and justified

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:26.760
China's adventures in expansion elsewhere.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.040
- [Male Reporter] This
is the South China Sea.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.260
- China says it will fight to the very end

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.720
to prevent Taiwan from
being declared independent.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.370
- [Male Reporter 2] The
former British colony

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.350
is being smashed into submissions.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.910
- So, now you have China building islands

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:39.930
in the South China Sea

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.600
claiming that this entire
ocean belongs to them.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.930
Oh, that's just China reclaiming
what was rightfully theirs,

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:46.763
because, after all,

00:16:46.763 --> 00:16:48.540
this ocean's been theirs for 5,000 years,

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:49.560
they're just reclaiming it.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.290
Violating its promise to let
Hong Kong stay independent

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.763
and absorbing it into
China piece by piece,

00:16:54.763 --> 00:16:57.570
oh, that's just China
restoring sovereignty

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.440
over these islands

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.750
that Britain stole in like the 1800s.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.870
How about an invasion of
Taiwan to unite it forcibly

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:04.703
with China?

00:17:04.703 --> 00:17:08.460
All they're doing is restoring
China back to the way it was.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.340
But, again, this was never the case.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.370
This is a story constructed 70 years ago

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.880
to unify a country that was
on the brink of collapse.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:20.580
This story today is weaponized

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:22.860
and used by Xi Jinping
and the communist party

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.597
to justify almost everything
that they're doing.

00:17:25.597 --> 00:17:28.110
- [Female Interpreter] A Xi
Jin national rejuvenation

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.453
will be no walk in the park.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.170
It will take more than drum beating

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.330
and the gong clanging to get there.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:37.590
Everyone of us in the party

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:41.010
must be prepared to work
even harder toward this goal.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:43.860
- Okay, so to end this, I
just wanna say one last thing,

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.950
which is I have no interest
in bashing on China

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:48.180
and Chinese culture.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.560
There is so much beauty

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:52.320
that comes from this region of the world.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:55.530
And, as I mentioned, every
one of the countries out there

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:56.363
including my own

00:17:56.363 --> 00:17:58.200
are guilty of a weaponized history.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.360
The reason I'm concerned
and focused on this

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:04.410
is because this mythical fake
story that China is using.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.390
It can't be fact checked within China.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.190
So, instead, the Chinese government

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:10.740
is able to use this story as a weapon

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:13.260
to justify the oppression of its people,

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.060
the grabbing of land,

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.530
and, honestly, looking at it,

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:17.370
how it's playing out,

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.500
it's just a modern day version

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:23.373
straight out of the old
European imperialistic handbook.

